Reason:
The function `fu_util_maybe_enable_automatic` incorrectly returned `TRUE` unconditionally when the case for `FU_UTIL_HISTORY_AUTOMATIC` was reached, without properly evaluating the conditions in the switch-case structure. This led to the function indicating success even when it should not, causing incorrect behavior during report uploading.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
break;
```
```c
return TRUE;
```
Reason:
The patch modifies the flow of the function by replacing the unconditional `return TRUE;` with a `break;` statement, allowing the function to exit the switch-case structure properly. This ensures that the function only returns `TRUE` after all conditions have been evaluated, thus fixing the logic error and preventing incorrect success indications during report uploading.


